lesson: 237
title: A deck of cards
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: A full deck of playing cards, without the jokers, has 52 cards: 4 suits of 13.
explain: When cards are dealt, each player gets the same number; the cards dealt are players × cards each.
explain: 4 players get 7 cards each from a full deck: 4 × 7 = 28 dealt, so 52 − 28 = 24 cards are left.
vars: a=name p=2..6 k=3..10
need: p * k <= 48
answer: 52 - p * k
exercise: {a} deals {k} cards to each of {p} players from a full deck. How many cards are left in the deck?
exercise: A full pack of cards is used. {p} players get {k} cards each. How many cards are left?
exercise: How many cards remain in a full deck after {k} cards are dealt to each of {p} players?
exercise: For a game, {a} gives {k} cards each to {p} players from a new deck without jokers. How many cards are not dealt?
exercise: Grandad deals {k} cards each to {p} of us from a full pack. How many cards are left in his hand?
exercise: {p} of us, {k} cards each from a full deck. how many left in the pile
exercise: dealt {k} cards each to {p+1}, no wait {p} players. full deck. how many left
exercise: full pack, {p} players get {k} each, oh and the jokers are already out. how many left
exercise: nan dealing rummy, {k} each, {p} of us. cards left over in the deck
exercise: {a} reckons {60-p*k} left after dealing {k} each to {p} players from a full deck. how many really
test: From a complete pack, {p} players are dealt {k} cards apiece. How big is the pile that remains?
test: {p} children each receive {k} cards from a new deck with no jokers. How many cards stay in the deck?
test: After a full deck has given {k} cards to every one of {p} players, how many cards are undealt?
test: full deck, {k} each, {p} players, whats left
test: we're {p}, {k} cards each, pack was full, no jokers. how many in the middle
test: A new pack of cards is opened and the jokers are thrown away. {p} players take {k} cards each. How many are left?
exam: Determine the number of cards remaining in a standard deck, jokers excluded, subsequent to the distribution of {k.words} cards to each of {p.words} players.
exam: It is given that {p} participants each receive {k} cards from a complete standard pack, the jokers having been removed. Ascertain the number of cards not distributed.
exam: Compute the residual quantity of cards in a full standard deck, exclusive of jokers, after {k} cards have been dealt to each of {p} players.
exam: Whereas a complete deck of playing cards, jokers excluded, is employed, and {p} players are each dealt {k} cards, state the number of cards remaining.
exercise: Grandma passed away and left her card table and a full deck to {a}'s family. {a} deals {k} cards to each of {p} players from her deck. How many cards are left in the deck?
exercise: my uncle got let go from the casino so now he deals at home, {k} cards each to {p} of us from a full pack. shut up and work out how many he's got left in his hand
test: {a} was economical with the truth when {a.he} said cards were missing: the pack is complete. {a.He} gives {p} people {k} cards apiece. How many cards remain undealt?
